 :finding {:id :s2b/full-size-ack-refused :classification :real-existing-contract-defect
           :evidence "Candidate record reports a frozen-valid 128-window baseline, awaiting owner, with exact matching ACK refused because the entire owned argument contains 4583 nodes. Candidate embeds event in snapshot command, pending projection, and owner reply; owned? counts map keys and repeated occurrences. Reported BB/NBB green suites do not cover that boundary; this plan does not independently rerun the measurement."
           :decision "Do not raise 4096 nodes, 65536 bytes or depth 32, truncate windows, weaken frozen validation, or frame this defect as needing fresh permission to support an already permitted 128-window event."}
 :recommendation {:name :versioned-compact-reference-witness-v1
  :principle "Use a closed, stateless, data-only wire/session representation with one lossless event arena and a reference-only state projection; never send the expanded state, event and witness together. The arena is owned input, not an owner ledger, authenticated store or durable authority. All projections and intents are derived by replay."
  :session "Closed {:format <version> :config <start-config> :events <packed-event-vector> :commands <compact-command-vector>}. Step accepts this session plus one closed compact input; start returns a session; freshness accepts session plus time. Responses return session and a small ref-based projection/intents, not another inline copy of the same arena. Exact field names/version to be specified in the descriptor and vocabulary; use only the eight permitted files."
  :event-arena "Store each semantically distinct event once. Assign small integer indices by first occurrence in the witness; no forward, dangling, duplicate or unused entries. Every snapshot/gap and ACK/resolution refers to its event index; an ACK must reference the exact current pending index, with predecessor, resulting head, revision, acceptance and generation checked by the existing core semantics. Resolve indices to immutable values before calling the core. Never substitute event ID or an unverified digest for full event equality. If hashing is used as an acceleration, collisions require full equality and hashes confer no authentication."
  :packed-events "Encode frozen snapshots losslessly with a versioned closed schema: common envelope/data fields retained once; a snapshot's 128 window maps become rows [xid incarnation workspace-index] plus an epoch field and a bounded dictionary of up to 32 distinct workspace UUIDs. Reconstruct every full window/key including epoch and workspace/id before safe/validate-event! and desktop/replay. Require exact closed shape, canonical integer and UUID representations, dictionary uniqueness and first-use ordering, no unused entries, and valid indices. Keep content/reference and every other legal envelope/data field losslessly; no guessing defaults or dropping causes. Gap events use their own closed lossless form. Encode the admitted JSON canonically with a bounded tokenizer."
  :projection "Derived projection contains head, phase, counters, lease, history event indices, pending/candidate index and other scalar fields; it is an output, not an input axiom. If an API retains an optional caller projection, compare it exactly to derived projection, excluding nothing semantically relevant. The event-bearing intent uses an index, and all non-index fields and bytes required to reconstruct the event remain available through the same session. Never compare a digest alone."
  :retention "Keep arena entries referenced by every represented snapshot, including abandoned or explicitly rejected candidates, as long as their commands are required for replay. They cannot be reconstructed from only current pending/history. Preserve entries for all subsequently accepted history and old gaps as well. Deduplicate only byte/structurally identical canonical events; never garbage-collect an entry still needed by replay. A reference with missing or altered event refuses rather than silently changing the trace."
  :trace "Replay from validated config with the existing single core transition function and bounded commands, reconstructing at event-use boundaries. Preserve exact generation/time, three-attempt count, ACK/head proof, accepted-before-loss, gap, reconciliation, and F3 post-cap resolution. Use lossless compact tuples for fixed command variants; compress repetitions only where proven semantically inert, tracking repeat count, monotonic time and budget. No supplied intermediate state or fabricated full trace implies external authenticity."
  :wire "This is an explicit versioned closed reference API, not an invisible semantic change to an existing full-state API. Bind descriptor, tests and edge codec to the new format; reject mixed or legacy forms unless explicitly supported without bypass. Result and next request must each obey fixed wire byte, node and depth limits. Product logic remains pure, with no external event fetch, callback or hidden mutable cache."}
 :budget-analysis {:counting "Frozen owned? counts map keys and values as nodes; edge JSON counter counts values differently. Both limits must independently pass. A frozen snapshot window entry has 11 owned nodes: outer map 1, two keys 2, inner three-entry window map 7, workspace value 1. Thus 128 entries alone cost 1408 nodes per expanded event, excluding its window vector, envelope and other fields."
                   :baseline-ack "A packed row has vector plus three scalar values = 4 nodes, or 512 nodes for 128 rows; a single arena event is shared by transcript, pending projection and ACK via integer references. Compare the reported 4583-node triple copy, not a claim that the candidate already supports the packed form."
                   :baseline-gap-reconcile "Two independently packed 128-window snapshots cost 1024 row nodes, versus at least 2816 for just their expanded window entries; the gap has a small fixed event record. Workspace dictionary adds at most 33 nodes per snapshot and no more than 32 UUIDs. The replay must check both full reconstructed events and exact causal gap link."
                   :abandoned "Three distinct maximum-window snapshots, possible across three attempts including abandoned/rejected ones, cost 1536 row nodes versus at least 4224 expanded window-entry nodes before any envelope or commands. First-use arena references retain all three without repeated full payload. With fixed-size command tuples, 256 commands also consume a bounded linear budget, but a blanket under-4096 guarantee for every legal trace is not established without measuring actual envelope, command arities, keys and optional fields."
                   :bytes "Rows still carry full incarnation UUIDs; dictionary indices avoid repeating workspace UUIDs. UUID payload alone for three 128-window snapshots is at least 13824 ASCII bytes before JSON punctuation, xids, optional fields, envelopes and commands. Do not infer full byte fit from node counts. Actual canonical encoded bytes, depth, nodes and reconstruction must be tested."
                   :universal-limit "Frozen event cause vectors and legal combinations may consume the remaining fixed frame budget; fixed scalar references cannot losslessly encode arbitrarily many distinct caller-provided identifiers in one finite frame. There is no honest guarantee that every individually valid event combined with every history fits a 65536-byte/4096-node stateless request. Explicitly fail closed on exceeding either bound without erasing pending facts. If an already required legal schedule cannot fit after this encoding, record the exact lower bound and seek a separately reviewed multi-frame protocol: a stateless verifier must receive all needed data for that invocation, and caller-supplied chunks/checkpoints alone are not authentication or proof of reachability. No silent new cap on 128-window events or history is authorized."}
 :red-oracles [{:id :reported-128 :assert "Generate frozen-valid 128 distinct windows, one workspace; drive start through both fences and pending. Exact matching ACK at legal time succeeds in BB and NBB and raw canonical edge, each request and result within all original caps; frozen replay and lease agree. Assert node and byte counts rather than just status."}
               {:id :full-gap-reconcile :assert "128-window baseline, valid admitted gap, 128-window reconciled baseline with fresh incarnations and exact causal link, including exact ACKs, succeeds through public boundary, both runtimes and edge. Check whole session plus current input and output sizes at each step, replay, history, active gap and freshness."}
               {:id :abandoned-snapshots :assert "Preserve a 128-window abandoned snapshot after represented loss and an explicitly rejected distinct 128-window candidate; then use a third distinct accepted 128-window snapshot if legal under three attempts. Replaying the returned witness must retain earlier arena values and reject missing/altered entries; prove bounds and canonical bytes at each stage."}
               {:id :identity-integrity :assert "Dangling, duplicate, unused, reordered or wrong event references, altered payload, wrong revision/head/predecessor, and any digest collision substitute deny without minting freshness or a competing intent. Projected current state and intents must equal replayed derivations."}
               {:id :stale-and-f3 :assert "After cap or deadline, exact bounded resolution of stale baseline, gap and reconciliation preserves pending identity and accounts accepted history without restoring freshness; unchanged-head rejection and wrong/untrusted evidence take the specified branches. No blind retry or competing event, and include loss/generation and no-op count fidelity."}
               {:id :edge-and-work :assert "Test 32-workspace dictionary, arbitrary legal optional fields and causes, 4096/4097 nodes, 65536/65537 bytes, depth 32/33, duplicates, canonical round trips, oversize failure without partial output, and BB/NBB parity. Instrument core transitions and frozen validation/replay; one replay is linear in records plus event work, with no recursive public validation or cubic trace replay. Record exact request/output counts and near-cap timing."}]
 :limits "Sizing arithmetic is derived from the immutable source and fixture shape, not new benchmark evidence. Full legal worst-case feasibility and F6 parser/descriptor settlement remain unverified; this plan does not approve candidate ab38 or the rest of S2B."
 :next "Implement this bounded reference representation and RED oracles within the existing file ceiling, then verify actual encoded budgets and request exact-head review."}
